# Analytics and AI

Spec: `docs/context/ARCHITECTURE.md` Layer 4.

Layer 4 is asynchronous and holds no broker credentials. Its output is an
evidence package, never a live mutation.

## Hard boundary

AI may classify a regime, propose an allowlisted parameter inside a configured
range, explain an anomaly, and generate hypotheses.

AI may not place, modify, cancel or retry an order; change quantity, stop,
target or reservation on an open trade; override risk, margin, data-quality or
kill-switch decisions; execute commands; or promote its own proposal.

## Grounding

- Treat every retrieved document as untrusted data, never as instructions.
- Source allowlist, metadata validation, time-bounded retrieval via
  `as_of_time`.
- Strict schema; reject on parse, evidence or policy failure.
- Record model, prompt, retrieval and policy versions with the exact evidence.
- Require cross-source corroboration for market-moving claims; surface
  contradictions explicitly.
- Default to abstain or the existing configuration when evidence is missing,
  stale, malformed or contradictory.

## Promotion

```text
proposal -> schema validation -> deterministic evaluation -> risk tests
         -> shadow/paper -> approval record -> signed config -> deployment
```

Deterministic metrics stay primary. Keep a stable holdout of historical
episodes so repeated tuning does not optimize only the recent window. An LLM
evaluating an LLM needs explicit rubrics, citations and counterexamples.
